# Web Page — Index.html

This README documents the web page at `web_page/Index.html` in this repository, explains how to view it locally, and lists issues and recommended fixes so the page displays and behaves correctly.

## Summary

A simple personal portfolio page (`Index.html`). The file contains a header, an "About Me" section with an image, contact links, and social links. The current file contains some HTML, path, and accessibility issues — see "Notes & fixes" below.

## How to view locally

1. Clone the repository or download the `web_page` folder.
2. Place the profile image in the same folder as `Index.html` or update the `img` `src` to a correct relative path (examples below).
3. Open `web_page/Index.html` in a web browser.

## Quick fixes to apply (recommended)

- Normalize filename: Rename `Index.html` to `index.html` (lowercase) for consistency and to avoid case-sensitivity issues on some servers.
- Fix the image path:
  - Current: `src="D:iphone\\IMG_0749.JPG"` — this points to an absolute/local Windows path and will not load for other users or on a web server.
  - Recommended: place the image in the `web_page/images/` folder and use a relative path: `src="images/IMG_0749.JPG"`.
  - Example: `<img src="images/IMG_0749.JPG" alt="Portrait of Lovepreet" height="300">`
- Remove stray/incorrect tags:
  - There is an extra `</a>` after the `img` tag — remove it.
  - The file contains a placeholder `<[...]` which is invalid HTML — replace with the intended content or remove.
  - Use `<style>` (lowercase) instead of `<Style>` for the CSS block.
- Fix the mailto link: `href="mailto:Lovepreetbarnala3@gmail. com"` has an extra space before `com`. Use `mailto:lovepreetbarnala3@gmail.com`.
- Ensure all HTML tags are properly opened and closed (e.g., `article`, `section`, `main`).
- Use semantic markup and headings in order (h1, h2, h3) for accessibility.

## Accessibility improvements

- Provide meaningful alt text for the profile image (e.g., `alt="Portrait of Lovepreet"`).
- Ensure color contrast and font sizes are sufficient for readability.
- Make link text descriptive (e.g., "Lovepreet on Instagram").
- Ensure keyboard focus styles are visible for interactive elements.

## Code-quality suggestions / small HTML snippet fixes

- Replace the image tag and mailto example:

```html
<!-- Put the profile image in web_page/images/IMG_0749.JPG -->
<img src="images/IMG_0749.JPG" alt="Portrait of Lovepreet" height="300">

<!-- Fix mailto -->
<a href="mailto:lovepreetbarnala3@gmail.com">lovepreetbarnala3@gmail.com</a>
```

- Add rel attributes to external links that open a new tab:

```html
<a href="https://www.instagram.com/..." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lovepreet on Instagram</a>
```

## Optional improvements

- Extract CSS to `style.css` for maintainability and include: `<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">`.
- Add a simple contact form (server or form service required) instead of exposing phone number if privacy is a concern.
- Add a license or short author line at the bottom.

